%U A399634 34592740,68670421,137357224,273152891,546338548,1087959661,2175984856,4337751875,8675634820,17308485061
%N A399634 a(n) is the number of ways to partition the first n positive integers into exactly three nonempty lists, each arranged in increasing order, such that no two adjacent integers within a list have the same parity.
%C A399634 Alternatively, a(n) is the number of ways to distribute n discs of distinct sizes among exactly three nonempty posts (towers), with the discs arranged in decreasing order of size from bottom to top, such that no two adjacent discs on the same post have the same color. The discs are initially arranged in a single tower in decreasing order of size, with colors alternating between black and white.
%H A399634 Janaka Rodrigo, <a href="/A399634/b399634.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..100</a>
%H A399634 Janaka Rodrigo, <a href="/A399634/a399634.txt">Python code for A399634</a>
%H A399634 <a href="/index/Rec#order_06">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (3,3,-15,4,18,-12).
%F A399634 From _Andrew Howroyd_, Nov 13 2026: (Start)
%F A399634 a(2*n+1) = 4^n + 3^n - 4*2^n + 2; a(2*n+2) = 2*(4^n + 3^n - 3*2^n + 1).
%F A399634 G.f.: x^3*(1 + x - 4*x^2 - 2*x^3)/((1 - x)*(1 - 2*x)*(1 - 2*x^2)*(1 - 3*x^2)). (End)
%F A399634 E.g.f.: (-1 + 12*cosh(x) + 3*cosh(2*x) - 18*cosh(sqrt(2)*x) + 4*cosh(sqrt(3)*x) + 12*sinh(x) + 6*cosh(x)*sinh(x) - 12*sqrt(2)*sinh(sqrt(2)*x) + 2*sqrt(3)*sinh(sqrt(3)*x))/6. - _Stefano Spezia_, Nov 13 2026
%e A399634 n = 5 has 11 different sets of 3 strings: {(1,2,3),(4),(5)}, {(1,2,5),(3),(4)}, {(1,4,5),(2),(3)}, {(2,3,4),(1),(5)}, {(3,4,5),(1),(2)}, {(1,2),(3,4),(5)}, {(1,2),(4,5),(3)}, {(1,4),(2,3),(5)}, {(1,4),(2,5),(3)}, {(2,3),(4,5),(1)}, {(2,5),(3,4),(1)}. Therefore a(5) = 11.
%Y A399634 Cf. A000392 (excluding parity restriction).
